Yes, 41 Burnside Lane is within the Burnside conservation area. It is not a listed building and has no tree preservation order.

The council's guidance says replacement windows in a conservation area need a planning application unless the new windows match the existing ones in material and pattern. So:

- If you want to replace the windows with the same material and design as the current ones, you may not need an application. I'd still suggest confirming that with the planning desk before you start.
- If the new windows will differ in material, style, or pattern, you will need to apply.

I can't give a formal opinion on your specific proposal. If you have an existing application reference for this property, send it over and I can look up its status.
